Attention mechanisms 

Attention allows a Transformer to determine which tokens are relevant to other tokens when computing their contextual representations.

 Query (Q): What information is this token looking for?
 Key (K): What information can this token be matched against?
 Value (V): What information can this token contribute?

Causal masking prevents a token from attending to future tokens.

Instead of calculating attention using only one set of Q, K, and V projections, Transformers use multiple attention heads.

Each head learns different projections and can capture different relationships between tokens.
